##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.0
# Spec 057 (area-light geometry), generated by specs/057-area-light-geometry/tools/gen_scenes.py: do not edit.
# AreaLight_QuadlightAgreement (US9, FR-022): examples/rib/quadlight.rib's geometry and light, the NEW form. The OLD form is the shipped
# quadlight shader; the NEW form is the same 2 x 2 quad as geometry under AreaLightSource "arealight" with the intensity divided by the
# quad's area (200 / 4 = 50: the shipped arealight returns I N.normalize(L) / (L.L) and the renderer adds A / n), 16 samples. Neither
# form shadows (quadlight's visibility() never occludes, GitHub #169; the sphere is not flagged transmission, so the new form's shadow
# rays pass through it): the sphere and the disk are plain receivers. Model difference: quadlight.sl takes the emitter cosine at the
# quad's CENTRE, the arealight at each sample point. The two renders are compared by the 8 x 8 block metric (the threshold is fixed after
# measurement, tasks.md T124).
version 3.03
Hider "raytrace"
Display "arealight-quadlight-agree-new-raytrace.tif" "file" "rgba"
Projection "perspective" "fov" 40
Format 320 240 1
Clipping 0.1 1000
Translate 0 0 12
WorldBegin
    AttributeBegin
        Attribute "arealight" "int samples" [16]
        AreaLightSource "arealight" 1 "float intensity" [50]
        Surface "constant"
        Polygon "P" [3 5 -2  5 5 -2  5 7 -2  3 7 -2]
    AttributeEnd
    Illuminate 1 1
    AttributeBegin
        Color [0.8 0.8 0.8]
        Surface "matte"
        Translate 0 0 3
        Sphere 1.5 -1.5 1.5 360
    AttributeEnd
    AttributeBegin
        Color [0.7 0.7 0.7]
        Surface "matte"
        Translate 0 -3 0
        Rotate -90 1 0 0
        Disk 0 20 360
    AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
